WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.657 --> 00:00:05.657
[cheerful reggae music]

00:00:11.549 --> 00:00:12.959
[Paul groaning]

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.144
- [Skateboarder] It's your
feet, your feet too big.

00:00:16.144 --> 00:00:17.677
- [Paul] It's too hot, man!

00:00:17.677 --> 00:00:18.861
- [Miloh] This is my roommate Paul.

00:00:18.861 --> 00:00:21.161
He's an easygoing, lovable,
fun but forgetful guy.

00:00:21.161 --> 00:00:22.973
That's where I come in to check him.

00:00:22.973 --> 00:00:25.372
[phone rings] Oop! That's me calling now.

00:00:25.372 --> 00:00:27.961
- What up, baby girl?

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.193
- Ew. Where are you?

00:00:30.193 --> 00:00:32.329
- Yeah, I'm out skating.

00:00:32.329 --> 00:00:34.093
- Oh, OK. Well, listen, don't forget.

00:00:34.093 --> 00:00:36.041
You're supposed to bring
home dinner tonight for us.

00:00:36.041 --> 00:00:36.741
- Yeah.

00:00:36.741 --> 00:00:39.849
- [Miloh] Uh, I'm broke
and Bo is definitely broke

00:00:39.849 --> 00:00:41.965
so make sure you bring home dinner.

00:00:41.965 --> 00:00:43.541
- Nah, I won't forget.

00:00:43.541 --> 00:00:46.096
- And do not bring home
Cups of Noodles and tomatoes

00:00:46.096 --> 00:00:47.629
again like you did last time,

00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:49.021
do no do that.

00:00:49.021 --> 00:00:50.320
- Yeah yeah yeah, don't do that again.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.156
- I'm, yep, I'm gonna get the food

00:00:52.156 --> 00:00:54.988
and you better make room for seconds.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:58.052
- All right. See you soon.

00:00:58.052 --> 00:01:00.608
- [Paul] Twenty-two dollars?

00:01:00.608 --> 00:01:02.652
[cash register bell
rings] 2 dollar draft fee?

00:01:02.652 --> 00:01:04.740
- [Miloh] Paul's gonna have
to stretch that twenty.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:05.668
- Fuck!

00:01:05.668 --> 00:01:10.668
[cheerful piano music]

00:01:18.183 --> 00:01:20.569
[cash register bell rings]

00:01:24.035 --> 00:01:25.544
- Hey, Paul.

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:27.356
- Hey Street Tim, what's going on?

00:01:27.356 --> 00:01:28.679
- Oh, what isn't?

00:01:28.679 --> 00:01:29.863
Did you hear the news?

00:01:29.863 --> 00:01:31.371
Drake's running for president.

00:01:31.371 --> 00:01:32.927
That means instead of a
Muslim we're gonna have

00:01:32.927 --> 00:01:34.275
a rapping-happing-hab.

00:01:34.275 --> 00:01:35.295
Tell me that's not progress.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.575
- That's not true.

00:01:36.575 --> 00:01:37.571
That's also offensive.

00:01:37.571 --> 00:01:38.851
- Ah, peas and carrots.

00:01:38.851 --> 00:01:40.615
You know, if you believe it,

00:01:40.615 --> 00:01:42.239
you can make it so.

00:01:42.239 --> 00:01:43.655
That's what I've learned.

00:01:43.655 --> 00:01:45.210
That's life.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.906
- That's good advice, man, thanks.

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.390
- So where're you headed off to?

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.458
You got any change for me?

00:01:49.458 --> 00:01:50.575
- Ah...

00:01:50.575 --> 00:01:52.642
- All right, it's nice talking to you.

00:01:52.642 --> 00:01:54.546
- All right, man.

00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:56.402
Tim!

00:01:56.402 --> 00:01:58.726
- Yeah?

00:01:58.726 --> 00:02:02.438
- Here's a dollar, buddy.
[cash register bell rings]

00:02:02.438 --> 00:02:04.202
That's all I got.

00:02:04.202 --> 00:02:05.482
- Well,

00:02:05.482 --> 00:02:06.733
Thanks, Paul.

00:02:06.733 --> 00:02:07.850
A whole dollar.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.589
I'm a millionaire.

00:02:09.589 --> 00:02:11.726
I'm a millionaire!

00:02:11.726 --> 00:02:13.842
- You sure are, Street Tim.

00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:15.766
You sure are.

00:02:15.766 --> 00:02:16.718
[bicycle bell rings]

00:02:16.718 --> 00:02:17.902
Crazy guy, ah!

00:02:17.902 --> 00:02:19.250
- [Cyclist] Sorry!

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.689
- Why would you do that?

00:02:20.689 --> 00:02:22.106
- How do I stop this thing?

00:02:22.106 --> 00:02:23.594
- Come back!

00:02:23.594 --> 00:02:27.536
Ah, now I need Obamacare.

00:02:28.817 --> 00:02:31.364
[screams]

00:02:34.249 --> 00:02:35.365
- Hey man.

00:02:35.365 --> 00:02:36.317
- [Cashier Jim] Oh, hey bro.

00:02:36.317 --> 00:02:37.501
- Can I get a Band-Aid?

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:38.149
- No.

00:02:38.149 --> 00:02:39.313
They come in a box, OK?

00:02:39.313 --> 00:02:40.657
I can't just give you one.

00:02:40.657 --> 00:02:42.096
They're called Band-Aids,

00:02:42.096 --> 00:02:43.489
not Band-Aid.

00:02:43.489 --> 00:02:44.513
- Well can you give me one

00:02:44.513 --> 00:02:46.021
from like a First Aid Kit or something?

00:02:46.021 --> 00:02:48.065
C'mon, I know you guys
have one back there.

00:02:48.065 --> 00:02:49.945
- No we don't.

00:02:49.945 --> 00:02:51.500
It's a myth.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:56.449
This is my shift and we
don't have a First Aid Kit.

00:02:56.449 --> 00:02:58.745
Ye shall not pass!

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.604
- Uh, Jim.

00:03:00.604 --> 00:03:01.672
Jim.

00:03:01.672 --> 00:03:03.040
Jim!

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.017
What'd I tell you about that

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:06.592
Game of Harry Potter
Thrones stuff here, man?

00:03:06.592 --> 00:03:08.615
No witchcraft on the shift.

00:03:08.615 --> 00:03:10.354
Now stop scaring the customers, man.

00:03:10.354 --> 00:03:13.259
- Sorry, Manager Larry.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:16.231
- Just gimme the Band-Aids,
bro, I'll take them.

00:03:16.231 --> 00:03:18.643
[scanner beeps] Five dollars?
[cash register bell rings]

00:03:18.643 --> 00:03:21.845
Are you serious?

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.579
Hey, can I get the rotisserie chicken

00:03:30.579 --> 00:03:32.762
and kale butternut squash?

00:03:32.762 --> 00:03:34.990
Thank you.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.802
Hey, man.

00:03:36.802 --> 00:03:37.962
What happened to the other guy?

00:03:37.962 --> 00:03:40.818
- Ah, he's on break so
you're stuck with me.

00:03:40.818 --> 00:03:42.258
It's gonna be $11.07.

00:03:42.258 --> 00:03:43.766
[cash register bell rings]

00:03:43.766 --> 00:03:44.858
- OK...

00:03:44.858 --> 00:03:46.274
- Hey man, this is gonna sound weird,

00:03:46.274 --> 00:03:48.946
but do you ever give money to
a guy named Tim on the street?

00:03:48.946 --> 00:03:50.153
- Yeah, I do.

00:03:50.153 --> 00:03:51.686
- That's my uncle.

00:03:51.686 --> 00:03:52.730
- No way.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:53.961
Street Tim is your uncle?

00:03:53.961 --> 00:03:55.770
- Yeah, man, as I live and breathe.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:57.674
Yeah, well he kinda lost it after 'Nam,

00:03:57.674 --> 00:03:59.070
and he likes to live on the street now

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.046
so we just kinda let him.

00:04:00.046 --> 00:04:01.694
I go down there and check
on him every now and then,

00:04:01.694 --> 00:04:02.762
give him something, make sure he's good.

00:04:02.762 --> 00:04:03.922
- Wow, dude, that's awesome.

00:04:03.922 --> 00:04:06.174
I love him, he's a good guy.

00:04:06.174 --> 00:04:08.078
- Hey you know what?

00:04:08.078 --> 00:04:09.377
This one's on me.

00:04:09.377 --> 00:04:10.769
- Are you sure, man? You
don't have to do that.

00:04:10.769 --> 00:04:12.233
- Trust me, dude, I've got this.

00:04:12.233 --> 00:04:13.234
Oh behalf of my uncle.

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:15.393
- Thank you so much, you have no...

00:04:15.393 --> 00:04:17.505
Thank you.

00:04:17.505 --> 00:04:19.525
I'm a millionaire!

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:20.917
It's something Street Tim...

00:04:20.917 --> 00:04:21.985
don't worry about it man.

00:04:21.985 --> 00:04:23.248
Thank you.

00:04:23.248 --> 00:04:25.011
- That's all right.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.346
He's a cool guy.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:32.817
[Bo cheers]

00:04:32.817 --> 00:04:34.093
- OK, deuces are wild...

00:04:34.093 --> 00:04:36.996
Hello, good evening.

00:04:36.996 --> 00:04:38.064
- Friends?

00:04:38.064 --> 00:04:39.064
- [Miloh] Yes?

00:04:39.064 --> 00:04:41.152
- I have dinner.

00:04:41.152 --> 00:04:44.172
- [Miloh] Oh no.

00:04:44.172 --> 00:04:45.516
- OK, so, Paul,

00:04:45.516 --> 00:04:47.120
we're no longer friends on Instagram.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.420
Or in real life, man.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.068
- [Paul] Yo yo, chill, chill, chill.

00:04:50.068 --> 00:04:51.788
I'm just joking, I'm just joking, look:

00:04:51.788 --> 00:04:53.364
Got some chicken, huh?

00:04:53.364 --> 00:04:55.967
Wash it down with some squash?

00:04:55.967 --> 00:04:57.659
You feel me? Some Band-Aids,

00:04:57.659 --> 00:04:59.031
those are mine.

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:00.611
But everything else we can eat, though.

00:05:00.611 --> 00:05:02.028
- Oh, the homie got a chicken,

00:05:02.028 --> 00:05:03.675
look at that, it even got
a little handle on it.

00:05:03.675 --> 00:05:05.671
Man, what you gonna eat though?

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:07.251
- I'mma eat that chicken.

00:05:07.251 --> 00:05:08.319
- No, you can have a wing, I guess.

00:05:08.319 --> 00:05:09.432
- You can have a wing.

00:05:09.432 --> 00:05:10.731
- Nah, I'm a breast man.

00:05:10.731 --> 00:05:12.255
Wait, how'd you know I want chicken?

00:05:12.255 --> 00:05:13.314
- [Miloh] Let's eat.

00:05:13.314 --> 00:05:14.747
I'm so proud of Paul.

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:15.757
Way to step up.

00:05:15.757 --> 00:05:17.419
He didn't tell us the story
of his day until later

00:05:17.419 --> 00:05:18.699
but it didn't matter by then

00:05:18.699 --> 00:05:22.197
because we were full and happy.

00:05:22.715 --> 00:05:27.445
[upbeat rap music]

00:05:30.887 --> 00:05:35.525
[film reel rolling]
[production theme music]

